  "limitations": [
    "Rust now performs the node allocation before Clone and releases uninitialized storage if Clone panics, matching OCCT placement-new/placement-delete ordering for this value-semantic fixture.",
    "Rust bucket arrays use Rust Vec storage rather than OCCT BaseAllocator arrays, so bucket allocation callbacks and capacity-growth effects remain different.",
    "C++ constructs the key directly in the IndexedMapNode base subobject; Rust Clone returns a complete key value that is then moved into the node. Address-sensitive C++ constructors and arbitrary subobject/destructor effects are not modeled.",
    "Allocator failure behavior, self-aliasing, and custom C++ constructor side effects beyond this trace are not proven.",
    "The checked-in Rust API snapshot predates add_ref; the retained private rustdoc capture resolves the path uniquely."
  ],
